JOHN I LIPP (lipp@mtu.edu) wrote:
: Suggestion for the next patchlevel of NH3.1:
: A genocide/wand of death or simular item should have no effect on
: 1)  Undead (zombies, wraiths, vampires, liches)
: 2)  Demons (especially the singular types)
: Why?  These criters are already dead!  Genocide implies death.  If it is already

Demons are not already dead.  They are extra-planar beings who have some
form of life force.

Although Zombies and skeletons are animated by means of magic only have
no life force, vampires and liches do have some sort of life, being
intelligent.  They are only partly alive.  Maybe death spells should only
inflict 1/2 damage.


: 1)  Wand of disintegration (superior version of wand of death, but 
:     anything the creature is carrying is gone too!  Also has limited 
:     digging ability.  Should  be as rare as W.O.W.)

I would argue that it should be as rare as a wand of cancellation,
because it has similar power.  That also would suggest a spellbook of
disintegration.  The spell would require 8 or 9 spell points
(cancellation requires 7) which would only allow you to read the
spellbook once.

